The valid review points are fixed. The suites pass, the zips are rebuilt, and nothing is committed.

**Verdicts.** I accepted all 11 points. Point 5 and point 7 were only partly valid. All 11 replies are under "## Kiro response" in `docs/reviews/s15-meta-review.md`.
- **Popup guide:** queued pages now take priority over `justSynced`. It clears when the queue hint shows or when pause is toggled.
- **`copySnippet`:** it now has the same guard as `copyMcp`.
- **Aria:** I removed `aria-hidden` from the units, which now read "seconds on them". I also removed `role="textbox"` from `#mcpUrl` and `#mcpSnippet`.
- **Dead strings:** I deleted 11 unused keys. A scan confirms every remaining key is used.
- **`.row` wrap:** it is now `.row.wrap`, applied only to the four button rows in Settings.
- **`siteBlocked`:** the count contract was fine, because `removed` is an object keyed by URL. I made the count defensive anyway and removed the trailing space.
- **Copy:**
  - Removed "watching", "haunt", "spook", "spirits", "Boo", "Keep it between us", "(I can wait)" and similar phrases.
  - The status pill now says "Remembering" instead of "Haunting".
  - Onboarding now says "I'll remember what you read, only for you."
  - Error messages are plain and each still says what to do next.
  - The forget-site error now says "Close and reopen the popup".
- **Tests:** I added a test that fails if any string contains the creepy words. I also added one for the `siteBlocked` trailing space and bad-count case. The e2e check label in `tests/e2e/run.mjs` no longer quotes the old "I'll be watching you" text.

**Not run.** The e2e suite did not run here, as in S15, because Chromium lacks system libraries.

**Tests.** The extension suite passes 45/45, up from 43. The worker suite passes 53/53, and the worker code is unchanged.

**Zips.** I rebuilt them with `build-chrome.mjs` and `build-firefox.mjs`. The chromium zip is copied byte-for-byte to `release/ghost-from-the-past-extension-v1.0.0.zip`, and `cmp` confirms they match. The new `lib/strings.js` is inside the zip.

**Docs.** I updated `.kiro/specs/ghost-mischief/tasks.md`, the s15 entry in `docs/kiro-logs/README.md`, and the README. The README now credits the Meta muse-spark review and says Kiro made the fixes. I also updated its extension test count to 45.

**To commit.** `extension/lib/strings.js` is still untracked, and `background.js` imports it. It must go into the same commit, or the service worker will fail to load.
